module rnaFragmentationDetection
module cdnaSynthesisDetection
module pcrProductDetection

manifest RNA_PBMC
manifest FragmentationBuffer
manifest StopSolution
manifest NucleaseFreeWater
manifest PrimerPP_RT
manifest MasterMixCDNA
manifest PrimerPP_TS
manifest PCRMasterMix
manifest PCRPrimers
manifest M13mp18_Template

// ============================================================
// A Solvent Replenishment Solution for Managing Evaporation
// of Biochemical Reactions in Air-Matrix Digital Microfluidics
// Jebrail, Renzi, Sinha et al., Sandia National Laboratories,
// Lab on a Chip (2015).
// DOI: 10.1039/C5LC00703H
//
// This file encodes the three DMF-mediated biochemical
// protocols demonstrated in the paper:
//
//   PROTOCOL 1 -- RNA Fragmentation
//     Reagents: 3 x 0.5 uL human PBMC total RNA (380 ng/uL)
//               + 0.5 uL 10X NEBNext fragmentation buffer
//               -> 2 uL reaction droplet
//     Temperature: 94 C, 3 min (= 180 s)
//     Evaporation replenishment: 6 x 0.5 uL nuclease-free water
//       added sequentially during incubation (just-in-time).
//     Termination: 4 C, 1 x 0.5 uL NEBNext stop solution.
//     QC: rnaFragmentationDetection (Bioanalyzer RNA Nano 6000)
//
//   PROTOCOL 2 -- First-Strand cDNA Synthesis (Peregrine)
//     Step A: 0.5 uL fragmented RNA + 0.5 uL primer PP_RT
//             incubated 65 C, 2 min (= 120 s), then 4 C.
//     Step B: 3 x 0.5 uL master mix merged; 25 C, 3 min (= 180 s),
//             then 42 C, 1 min (= 60 s).
//     Step C: 0.5 uL primer PP_TS merged; 42 C, 60 min (= 3600 s).
//             Evaporation replenishment: 9 x 0.5 uL water during
//             42 C 60-min incubation.
//     Step D: termination: 70 C, 5 min (= 300 s).
//             Evaporation replenishment: 4 x 0.5 uL water during
//             termination incubation.
//     QC: cdnaSynthesisDetection (qPCR Ct assay + Bioanalyzer)
//
//   PROTOCOL 3 -- PCR (M13mp18 template, 200 bp amplicon)
//     Reagents: 0.5 uL PCR master mix + 0.5 uL primers
//               + 0.5 uL M13mp18 template -> 1.5 uL droplet
//     Cycling: 95 C 45 s; 33 x (95 C 20 s, 50 C 30 s, 68 C 45 s);
//              68 C 5 min (= 300 s).
//     Cycling modelled as sequential heat steps (see note below).
//     Evaporation replenishment: 1 x 0.5 uL water per cycle
//       (33 total); modelled as 33 chained dispense+mix steps
//       between the two heat blocks.
//     QC: pcrProductDetection (gel electrophoresis, 200 bp band)
//
// DEVICE: 6-layer PCB, 100 actuation electrodes (1.6x1.6 mm),
//   7 fluid reservoirs, 4 TEC thermal zones, 4 RTD sensors.
//   Top plate: ITO on glass coated with 50 nm Teflon-AF.
//   Bottom plate: Cu/Ni/Au electrodes, 50 nm Teflon-AF.
//   Gap spacing: 185 um (RNA fragmentation, cDNA) or 800 um (PCR).
//   Driving potential: 80-100 Vrms, 18 kHz.
//   Through-hole (0.8 mm ID) for replenishing droplet delivery
//   via PEEK tubing from external syringe pump.
//
// EVAPORATION REPLENISHMENT ABSTRACTION:
//   The paper's central innovation is "just-in-time" merging of
//   pre-heated solvent droplets to counteract evaporation during
//   high-temperature incubations. In BioScript, each replenishment
//   event is modelled as:
//     waterN = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
//     rxnDroplet = mix rxnDroplet with waterN for 5s
//   This captures: (1) dispensing from the through-hole syringe
//   reservoir onto the DMF surface; (2) transport to the thermal
//   zone edge for pre-heating (5 s abstracted into mix duration);
//   (3) merging with the reaction droplet to restore volume.
//   The 15-20% volume loss threshold and <=1 C temperature change
//   on merging are physical constraints handled by the TEC control
//   board and cannot be represented in BioScript primitives.
//
// TEMPERATURE TRANSITIONS:
//   Rapid temperature change is achieved by shuttling the reaction
//   droplet between thermal zones set to different temperatures.
//   Each `heat` statement models one steady-state incubation phase;
//   droplet transport between zones is implicit between statements.
//
// PCR CYCLING NOTE:
//   BioScript has no loop primitive. The 33 PCR cycles are encoded
//   as two heat blocks (denaturation and anneal/extend phases)
//   with the 33 interleaved replenishment steps between them.
//   This is a necessary abstraction; the compiler will emit a
//   linear CFG rather than a cyclic one, which correctly captures
//   the sequential electrode actuation schedule.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main             -- entry: RNA fragmentation protocol
//   BB2  rnaPass          -- rnaSignal > 0: valid fragments;
//                            dispose reaction droplet
//   BB3  rnaFail          -- rnaSignal <= 0: fragmentation failed;
//                            drain reaction droplet
//   BB4  rnaJoin          -- join: cDNA synthesis branch begins
//   BB5  cdnaPass         -- cdnaSignal > 0: valid cDNA yield;
//                            dispose reaction droplet
//   BB6  cdnaFail         -- cdnaSignal <= 0: synthesis failed;
//                            drain reaction droplet
//   BB7  cdnaJoin         -- join: PCR branch begins
//   BB8  pcrPass          -- pcrSignal > 0: correct 200 bp band;
//                            dispose PCR droplet
//   BB9  pcrFail          -- pcrSignal <= 0: no product; drain
//   BB10 finalCleanup     -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 1: Dispense RNA sample droplets.
//   Three independent 0.5 uL droplets of human PBMC total RNA
//   (380 ng/uL each) dispensed from their reservoir.
//   Paper M&M: "three 0.5 uL droplets of human PBMC total RNA
//   (each 380 ng/uL)."
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rna1 = dispense 1 units of RNA_PBMC
rna2 = dispense 1 units of RNA_PBMC
rna3 = dispense 1 units of RNA_PBMC

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 2: Dispense fragmentation buffer droplet.
//   0.5 uL 10X NEBNext fragmentation buffer dispensed from
//   its reservoir. Will be merged with all three RNA droplets.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

fragBuffer = dispense 1 units of FragmentationBuffer

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 3: Merge all reagents into reaction droplet.
//   Merge the three RNA droplets and fragmentation buffer
//   sequentially. On-chip mixing for 10 s per merge step.
//   Final reaction droplet: 2 uL (4 x 0.5 uL).
//   Paper M&M: "mixed together on the DMF device surface"
//   and "transported to a thermal zone."
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rnaMix1   = mix rna1 with rna2 for 10s
rnaMix2   = mix rnaMix1 with rna3 for 10s
rnaRxn    = mix rnaMix2 with fragBuffer for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 4: Incubate at 94 C for 3 min (= 180 s).
//   Thermal fragmentation of RNA. Droplet transported to
//   thermal zone (94 C). TEC closed-loop PID control.
//   Without replenishment, droplet dries in <2 min (paper).
//   `heat` is void/in-place; rnaRxn variable persists.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat rnaRxn at 94c for 180s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 5: Evaporation replenishment (6 water
//   droplets). Six 0.5 uL nuclease-free water droplets are
//   delivered just-in-time through the through-hole syringe
//   interface, pre-heated at the thermal zone edge, and merged
//   to restore reaction volume (paper: 6 total replenishments
//   over 3 min at 94 C; replenish when volume drops 15-20%).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

w1_rna = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
rnaRxn = mix rnaRxn with w1_rna for 5s

w2_rna = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
rnaRxn = mix rnaRxn with w2_rna for 5s

w3_rna = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
rnaRxn = mix rnaRxn with w3_rna for 5s

w4_rna = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
rnaRxn = mix rnaRxn with w4_rna for 5s

w5_rna = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
rnaRxn = mix rnaRxn with w5_rna for 5s

w6_rna = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
rnaRxn = mix rnaRxn with w6_rna for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 6: Cool to 4 C and add stop solution.
//   Droplet shuttled to the 4 C thermal zone to terminate
//   fragmentation. 0.5 uL NEBNext stop solution dispensed
//   and merged with the cooled reaction droplet.
//   Paper M&M: "cooled to 4 C, and RNA fragmentation was
//   terminated by supplementing the reaction with a 0.5 uL
//   droplet of NEBNext stop solution."
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat rnaRxn at 4c for 30s

stopSol   = dispense 1 units of StopSolution
rnaRxn    = mix rnaRxn with stopSol for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 7: QC detection.
//   rnaFragmentationDetection abstracts offline fragment-size
//   analysis (Agilent 2100 Bioanalyzer, RNA Nano 6000 Chip).
//   Expected: fragments predominantly 40-1000 nt, peak ~150 nt,
//   no residual 18S/28S rRNA peaks.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rnaSignal = detect rnaFragmentationDetection on rnaRxn for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: RNA fragmentation QC gate
// Pass (BB2): rnaSignal > 0 -> valid fragment distribution;
//             dispose reaction droplet.
// Fail (BB3): rnaSignal <= 0 -> fragmentation failed; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (rnaJoin).
// ============================================================

if (rnaSignal > 0) {
    dispose rnaRxn
} else {
    drain rnaRxn
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: rnaJoin
// Dispose RNA QC signal droplet. Control falls into the
// cDNA synthesis branch (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose rnaSignal

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 2: First-Strand cDNA Synthesis (Peregrine Method)
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 2 - STEP 1 (Step A): Dispense fragmented RNA and
//   primer PP_RT.
//   0.5 uL fragmented human PBMC total RNA (100 ng) and
//   0.5 uL primer PP_RT (25 mM) dispensed from reservoirs,
//   merged and mixed on DMF surface.
//   Paper M&M: "a 0.5 uL droplet of fragmented human PBMC
//   total RNA (100 ng) and a 0.5 uL droplet of primer PP_RT
//   (25 mM) were dispensed from their respective reservoirs,
//   merged and mixed."
// ------------------------------------------------------------

fragRNA   = dispense 1 units of RNA_PBMC
ppRT      = dispense 1 units of PrimerPP_RT

cdnaRxn   = mix fragRNA with ppRT for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 2 - STEP 2 (Step A cont.): Denaturation at 65 C,
//   2 min (= 120 s), then immediately cool to 4 C.
//   Denatures RNA secondary structure for efficient priming.
//   Transport to 65 C zone, then 4 C zone.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat cdnaRxn at 65c for 120s
heat cdnaRxn at 4c for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 2 - STEP 3 (Step B): Merge master mix droplets.
//   Three 0.5 uL master mix droplets (45% 5X First-Strand
//   Buffer, 5.5% 20 mM DTT, 22% 10 mM dNTP mix, 5.5%
//   RiboGuard RNase inhibitor, 22% SMARTScribe RT, 0.1%
//   Pluronics F-127 w/v) dispensed and merged sequentially.
//   Paper M&M: "three droplets of master mix [0.5 uL each]
//   were dispensed onto the DMF surface, merged with the
//   1 uL droplet."
// ------------------------------------------------------------

mm1 = dispense 1 units of MasterMixCDNA
mm2 = dispense 1 units of MasterMixCDNA
mm3 = dispense 1 units of MasterMixCDNA

mmCombined = mix mm1 with mm2 for 5s
mmCombined = mix mmCombined with mm3 for 5s
cdnaRxn    = mix cdnaRxn with mmCombined for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 2 - STEP 4 (Step B cont.): Incubate at 25 C (RT)
//   for 3 min (= 180 s), then 42 C for 1 min (= 60 s).
//   RT incubation: primer annealing to fragmented RNA template.
//   42 C incubation: reverse transcriptase activation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat cdnaRxn at 25c for 180s
heat cdnaRxn at 42c for 60s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 2 - STEP 5 (Step C): Merge primer PP_TS.
//   0.5 uL of primer PP_TS (12 mM) dispensed and merged with
//   the reaction droplet.
//   Paper M&M: "a 0.5 uL droplet of primer PP_TS (12 mM)
//   was merged with the reaction droplet."
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ppTS    = dispense 1 units of PrimerPP_TS
cdnaRxn = mix cdnaRxn with ppTS for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 2 - STEP 6 (Step C cont.): Incubate at 42 C for
//   60 min (= 3600 s). SMARTScribe RT template-switching and
//   extension. Reaction volume maintained by evaporation
//   replenishment (9 x 0.5 uL water, paper M&M: "nine
//   replenishing droplets were added during the incubation
//   at 42 C for 1 h").
//   NOTE: heat first, then replenishment events modelled
//   as interleaved dispense+mix steps below.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat cdnaRxn at 42c for 3600s

// Evaporation replenishment: 9 water droplets during 42 C / 1 h
w1_cdna = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
cdnaRxn = mix cdnaRxn with w1_cdna for 5s

w2_cdna = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
cdnaRxn = mix cdnaRxn with w2_cdna for 5s

w3_cdna = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
cdnaRxn = mix cdnaRxn with w3_cdna for 5s

w4_cdna = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
cdnaRxn = mix cdnaRxn with w4_cdna for 5s

w5_cdna = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
cdnaRxn = mix cdnaRxn with w5_cdna for 5s

w6_cdna = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
cdnaRxn = mix cdnaRxn with w6_cdna for 5s

w7_cdna = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
cdnaRxn = mix cdnaRxn with w7_cdna for 5s

w8_cdna = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
cdnaRxn = mix cdnaRxn with w8_cdna for 5s

w9_cdna = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
cdnaRxn = mix cdnaRxn with w9_cdna for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 2 - STEP 7 (Step D): Termination at 70 C, 5 min
//   (= 300 s). Inactivates SMARTScribe RT. 4 x 0.5 uL water
//   replenishments during this incubation.
//   Paper M&M: "the reaction was terminated by incubating at
//   70 C for 5 min ... four [replenishing droplets] during
//   the incubation at 70 C."
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat cdnaRxn at 70c for 300s

// Evaporation replenishment: 4 water droplets during 70 C / 5 min
w10_cdna = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
cdnaRxn  = mix cdnaRxn with w10_cdna for 5s

w11_cdna = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
cdnaRxn  = mix cdnaRxn with w11_cdna for 5s

w12_cdna = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
cdnaRxn  = mix cdnaRxn with w12_cdna for 5s

w13_cdna = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
cdnaRxn  = mix cdnaRxn with w13_cdna for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 2 - STEP 8: QC detection.
//   cdnaSynthesisDetection abstracts the qPCR Ct assay
//   (SsoFast EvaGreen, primers PP_P1/PP_P2, CFX96; 95 C 45 s,
//   25 x [95 C 5 s, 60 C 30 s]) and Bioanalyzer High
//   Sensitivity DNA Assay Chip readout of ds-cDNA libraries.
//   Expected: Ct comparable to conventional benchscale;
//   ds-cDNA size profile indistinguishable from control.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cdnaSignal = detect cdnaSynthesisDetection on cdnaRxn for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: cDNA synthesis QC gate
// Pass (BB5): cdnaSignal > 0 -> valid cDNA yield; dispose.
// Fail (BB6): cdnaSignal <= 0 -> synthesis failed; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (cdnaJoin).
// ============================================================

if (cdnaSignal > 0) {
    dispose cdnaRxn
} else {
    drain cdnaRxn
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: cdnaJoin
// Dispose cDNA QC signal. Control falls into PCR branch
// (BB8/BB9).
// ============================================================

dispose cdnaSignal

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 3: PCR (Bacteriophage M13mp18, 200 bp amplicon)
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 3 - STEP 1: Dispense PCR reagent droplets.
//   Three 0.5 uL droplets:
//     (a) PCR master mix: Hot Start Taq 2X MM + 2x extra Taq
//         (0.025 U/uL Hot Start Taq in 2X MM; doubled Taq).
//     (b) Primers: forward TGTTAATACTGACCGCCTCAC +
//         reverse CAGTAATAAAAGGGACATTCTGGC; 200 bp amplicon
//         spanning positions 4905-5104 of M13mp18 (X02513.1);
//         mixed equimolar, 4 uM per primer in 4X stock -> 2 uM final.
//     (c) Template: M13mp18 ssDNA, 250 pg/uL.
//   All three dispensed from separate reservoirs.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pcrMM       = dispense 1 units of PCRMasterMix
pcrPrimers  = dispense 1 units of PCRPrimers
pcrTemplate = dispense 1 units of M13mp18_Template

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 3 - STEP 2: Merge PCR reagents into reaction droplet.
//   Paper M&M: "droplets of master mix, primers, and template
//   (0.5 uL each) were dispensed from their respective
//   reservoirs, merged and mixed on the DMF surface."
//   Final 1.5 uL droplet transported to thermal zone.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pcrMix1 = mix pcrMM with pcrPrimers for 5s
pcrRxn  = mix pcrMix1 with pcrTemplate for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 3 - STEP 3: Initial denaturation: 95 C, 45 s.
//   Hot Start Taq activation. Droplet shuttled to 95 C zone.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat pcrRxn at 95c for 45s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 3 - STEP 4: 33 PCR cycles.
//   Cycling profile per cycle:
//     Denaturation: 95 C, 20 s
//     Annealing:    50 C, 30 s (Tm of primers ~57-60 C)
//     Extension:    68 C, 45 s (~1 kb/min Hot Start Taq rate)
//
//   Replenishment: 1 x 0.5 uL water added per cycle after
//   the 95 C denaturation step (paper: "adding one droplet
//   upon completion of each temperature cycle").
//
//   BioScript has no loop construct. All 33 cycles are encoded
//   as sequential denaturation + anneal/extend heat blocks with
//   one interleaved replenishment step per cycle.
//
//   NOTE ON HEAT BLOCK GROUPING:
//   The two intra-cycle temperatures (50 C and 68 C) are encoded
//   together as one anneal block followed by one extend block
//   to keep per-cycle structure clear. Denaturation (95 C)
//   is separated so the replenishment water dispense can be
//   inserted between denaturation and anneal/extend.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// -- Cycle 1 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR01 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR01 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 2 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR02 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR02 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 3 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR03 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR03 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 4 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR04 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR04 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 5 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR05 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR05 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 6 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR06 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR06 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 7 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR07 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR07 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 8 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR08 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR08 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 9 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR09 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR09 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 10 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR10 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR10 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 11 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR11 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR11 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 12 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR12 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR12 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 13 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR13 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR13 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 14 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR14 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR14 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 15 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR15 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR15 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 16 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR16 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR16 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 17 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR17 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR17 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 18 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR18 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR18 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 19 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR19 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR19 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 20 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR20 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR20 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 21 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR21 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR21 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 22 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR22 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR22 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 23 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR23 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR23 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 24 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR24 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR24 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 25 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR25 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR25 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 26 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR26 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR26 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 27 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR27 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR27 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 28 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR28 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR28 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 29 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR29 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR29 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 30 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR30 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR30 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 31 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR31 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR31 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 32 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR32 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR32 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// -- Cycle 33 --
heat pcrRxn at 95c for 20s
wPCR33 = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater
pcrRxn = mix pcrRxn with wPCR33 for 5s
heat pcrRxn at 50c for 30s
heat pcrRxn at 68c for 45s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 3 - STEP 5: Final extension: 68 C, 5 min (= 300 s).
//   Completes all partially extended amplicons. Paper: "and
//   finally 68 C for 5 min." No additional replenishment
//   events specified for this step in the paper.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat pcrRxn at 68c for 300s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 3 - STEP 6: QC detection.
//   pcrProductDetection abstracts gel electrophoresis readout
//   (2% agarose E-Gel system, Life Technologies).
//   Expected: single band at 200 bp comparable to conventional
//   PCR; slightly reduced yield vs. benchscale acceptable.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pcrSignal = detect pcrProductDetection on pcrRxn for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: PCR product QC gate
// Pass (BB8): pcrSignal > 0 -> 200 bp product detected;
//             dispose PCR reaction droplet.
// Fail (BB9): pcrSignal <= 0 -> no product; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (pcrSignal > 0) {
    dispose pcrRxn
} else {
    drain pcrRxn
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all three QC signal droplets. Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose pcrSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
